# Click to focus. A Standard game, four half-turns (1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6), then Home: the Overview of five boards at zoom ~0.78 (< 0.8).
# A single click on a square below zoom 0.8 focuses that board (zoom 1.0) and selects the piece in one motion; Esc steps back: the
# selection first, then the framing. A click on a card's label strip, or on a board that is history, focuses that board.
# Layout (1400x800): Versus (150,250); Standard row (905,224); Play (808,712); Submit (841,90).
wait 20
click 150 250        # Versus
wait 30
click 905 224        # Standard
wait 20
click 808 712        # Play
wait 120
clicksq 0 0 e2
wait 30
clicksq 0 0 e4
wait 30
click 841 90         # Submit
wait 60
clicksq 0 1 e7
wait 30
clicksq 0 1 e5
wait 30
click 841 90
wait 60
clicksq 0 2 g1
wait 30
clicksq 0 2 f3
wait 30
click 841 90
wait 60
clicksq 0 3 b8
wait 30
clicksq 0 3 c6
wait 30
click 841 90
wait 60
key HOME
wait 40
camexpect state Overview
camexpect zoom 0.5 0.79
capture camera-click-focus-overview
clicksq 0 4 f3       # the white knight on a board too small to read: the camera comes up and the piece is picked up
wait 40
camexpect state Focus
camexpect zoom 0.99 1.01
camexpect visible 0 4
capture camera-click-focus-piece-selected
key ESCAPE           # step 1: the selection goes, the framing stays
wait 20
camexpect state Focus
capture camera-click-focus-esc-selection
key ESCAPE           # step 2: back to the Overview
wait 40
camexpect state Overview
capture camera-click-focus-esc-overview
clickcard 0 1        # the label strip of a board that is history
wait 40
camexpect state Focus
camexpect visible 0 1
capture camera-click-focus-card-chrome
key HOME
wait 40
clicksq 0 2 d5       # an empty square of a past board: focus it, nothing is selected
wait 40
camexpect state Focus
camexpect visible 0 2
capture camera-click-focus-past-board
